# Guess That Tune playlist backups

Backups are generated by `backup.py`, which writes the same format as the
backup tool in the `spotify-explore` app.

## Create the backups

Sign in to [spotify_player](https://github.com/aome510/spotify-player) with
the owner Spotify account, then run from this repository:

```sh
python3 backup.py
```

The script uses spotify_player's cached login and only reads from Spotify. It
overwrites the backup files in this repository; review the changes before
committing them. It writes nothing if any playlist comes back more than 20%
smaller than its current backup.

## Monthly schedule

The LaunchAgent `com.benshaw.playlist-backup` runs `scripts/run-backup.zsh` at
9:00 AM on the 14th of each month, the day before the album radar and taste
discovery jobs read these files. On `master` it commits the refreshed backups
and pushes them; on any other branch it only writes the files. If Spotify
rate-limits the run it fails without touching the backups. Install or
reinstall it with:

```sh
scripts/install-launchd.zsh
```

`launchd/com.benshaw.playlist-backup.plist` is a template; the installer fills
in the local paths, so the installed job is a copy rather than a symlink. Logs
go to `logs/`, which isn't committed.

The playlists it backs up are listed in `PLAYLISTS` at the top of the script.
`Ben's Liked Songs` is the account's Liked Songs, which isn't a real playlist,
so its files show `Playlist ID: liked`. Before October 2026 it was backed up by
copying Liked Songs into the `Ben's Music` playlist
(`23nFRTPMFPAEX5UJohI8Xx`) first.
